From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:16:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: build against the Vulkan 1.4.363 headers and registry

Mesa 26.2.6 bundles the Vulkan 1.4.354 headers and registry. The Venus
codec is generated from the SDK registry that tools/rootfs/vulkan pins,
and the 1.4.363 registry names VkPhysicalDevicePipelineLibraryGroup
HandlesFeaturesKHR and VkPrivateDataSlotCreateFlagBits, which the
bundled headers lack. The guest driver, and the Android port that
compiles the same sources against the same bundled headers, therefore
failed to build with the generated codec.

Replace include/vulkan, include/vk_video and src/vulkan/registry/vk.xml
with the files of Vulkan-Headers sdk-1.4.363.0, the SDK the codec, the
renderer and the guest Vulkan-Loader are built from. Only
vk_android_native_buffer.h, which the SDK does not carry, stays. The
drivers report VK_HEADER_VERSION as their API patch level, so the guest
and KosmicKrisp now report 1.4.363, as the Loader does.

The registry needs two generator allowances, as earlier registry moves
did. VK_EXT_cooperative_matrix_maintenance1 repeats three features of
VK_NV_cooperative_matrix2, so the NV names are renamed apart. Nine SPIR-V
capabilities of the new registry are not in the SPIR-V headers Mesa
bundles yet, so the capability generator skips them until those move.

A change to the pinned SDK needs this topic refreshed from it; the
Vulkan sealer refuses a Mesa whose bundled registry differs from the
pinned one.
